Inventory of the 81 packages in the Cargo.lock all-target dependency graph, with
160 original license texts. Resolved features were refreshed from `cargo metadata` on
2026-11-03, when the crates only the removed demos used (ratatui, crossterm, sha2 and their
dependencies) left the graph; sha2 and its eight dependencies came back that day,
to fingerprint approved project agents, with the texts reproduced from the cached sources.
image and its 22 dependencies joined the graph the same day, for images the read tool sends,
with the texts reproduced from the cached sources and two embedded notices their sources
carry: color_quant's (NeuQuant) and image's JPEG encoder's, from the Independent JPEG Group's
libjpeg. This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group.
pulldown-cmark and its dependencies pulldown-cmark-escape and unicase joined the graph
the same day, for the web page /export writes, with the texts reproduced from the cached
sources; memchr's `default` feature is resolved since then.
sha2's asm features are not enabled; its inactive aarch64 sources say "Implementation
adapted from mbedtls" without naming its revision or license: re-audit before enabling asm.
version_check and autocfg are build dependencies, not evidence of runtime shipment.
zlib-rs is locked only through flate2's weak `zlib-rs?/std` feature and is not built
(`cargo tree --target all -i zlib-rs` prints nothing); its sources were not audited for
embedded notices.
Root license texts and embedded notices are reproduced below.
This inventory is not a legal clearance guarantee. libc 0.2.190 identifies
standard ioctl ABI helpers adapted from a GPL-2.0-tagged Linux Rust file;
the equivalent UAPI header has Linux-syscall-note. Upstream publishes the crate
under MIT OR Apache-2.0. The qualified provenance review is in Git history
(`git show d5ae40e:docs/PROGRESS-ARCHIVE.md`).
The application itself incorporates no copied kernel implementation.


